## Why This Is Asked
Tests understanding of cross-account temporary access, least-privilege IAM policies, and time-bound credentials using STS.

## Key Concepts
- Cross-account trust via AssumeRole
- Least privilege scoped to a specific S3 prefix
- Role duration controls expiry
- Testing access during and after the window

## Code Example
```json
// Trust policy (for the role in OUR account)
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Principal": {"AWS": "arn:aws:iam::PARTNER_ACCOUNT_ID:root"},
      "Action": "sts:AssumeRole"
    }
  ]
}
```
```json
// Role policy (least privilege for PIX123)
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Action": ["s3:ListBucket"],
      "Resource": "arn:aws:s3:::shared-docs",
      "Condition": {"StringLike": {"s3:prefix": ["contracts/PIX123/*"]}}
    },
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Action": ["s3:GetObject"],
      "Resource": "arn:aws:s3:::shared-docs/contracts/PIX123/*"
    }
  ]
}
```

